WEBVTT

00:01.795 --> 00:03.797
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:29.781 --> 00:33.827
(OMINOUS MUSIC INTENSIFIES, SPEEDS UP)

00:34.786 --> 00:35.787
(OMINOUS MUSIC ENDS)

00:39.040 --> 00:40.291
- (WATER DRIPPING)
- (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:40.375 --> 00:42.377
(WOMAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

00:44.337 --> 00:45.338
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

01:10.280 --> 01:11.322
(WOMAN 2 SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

01:14.617 --> 01:16.202
(WOMAN WHIMPERING)

01:18.538 --> 01:19.539
(WOMAN 2 SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

01:31.426 --> 01:33.428
- (ROPE CREAKING)
- (CHOKING)

01:35.263 --> 01:36.598
(WOMAN 2 CONTINUES IN RUSSIAN)

01:40.393 --> 01:41.394
(CHOKES)

01:45.356 --> 01:47.192
(WOMAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

01:47.275 --> 01:49.277
(OMINOUS MUSIC INTENSIFYING)

01:52.655 --> 01:54.157
(MUSIC STOPS)

01:56.993 --> 01:58.745
- (WATER SLOSHING)
- (MUFFLED CHATTER)

02:04.626 --> 02:06.085
(ENGINE REVVING)

02:06.169 --> 02:07.378
(GIRLS LAUGHING)

02:08.755 --> 02:09.756
GIRL 1: No way.

02:09.839 --> 02:10.924
That's so crazy.

02:11.007 --> 02:12.008
GIRL 2: No, you have had Snapchat.

02:12.091 --> 02:13.468
GIRL 1: I'm not on there. Are you on it?

02:13.551 --> 02:14.552
GIRL 3: No.

02:14.636 --> 02:15.929
(GIRL 3 GIGGLES)

02:16.012 --> 02:17.680
No! There's no way...

02:17.764 --> 02:19.474
GIRL 1: I'm so jealous! Yeah.
GIRL 3:...she posted that.

02:19.557 --> 02:21.059
GIRL 1: She'd be so embarrassed.

02:21.142 --> 02:22.811
GIRL 3: No, the fact that
she's trying to be you, but...

02:22.894 --> 02:24.103
GIRL 2:...she's like a millennial!

02:24.187 --> 02:25.688
GIRL 3: Yeah, she genuinely is.

02:25.772 --> 02:27.232
Hey, are you guys going to the city?

02:28.900 --> 02:29.901
Yeah.

02:30.860 --> 02:32.570
You meeting some friends there?

02:33.988 --> 02:35.156
GIRL 1: Yeah.

02:35.657 --> 02:36.658
GIRL 2: Why?

02:36.741 --> 02:37.784
BOY: Piper!

02:38.785 --> 02:39.994
You were supposed to wait for me.

02:41.329 --> 02:42.997
- I don't know who this is.
- (BOY SIGHS)

02:43.081 --> 02:44.791
- Such a pedophile.
- I'm not... What the...

02:44.874 --> 02:46.209
I'm her brother.

02:46.918 --> 02:48.336
Uh, stepbrother.

02:48.419 --> 02:50.255
Um, Kimmy.

02:50.922 --> 02:52.799
- Let's go.
- KIMMY: Oh, thank God.

02:54.467 --> 02:55.468
BOY: Okay.

02:57.470 --> 02:58.555
- Come on.
- (GIRLS GIGGLING)

02:58.638 --> 02:59.931
They didn't like me, did they?

03:02.392 --> 03:03.977
(MOCKINGLY) "Are you guys
going to the city?"

03:05.436 --> 03:07.355
BOY: No, no, they liked you.

03:07.438 --> 03:09.274
- No, they didn't.
- No, they did, they did.

03:10.108 --> 03:11.484
There was three of them

03:11.568 --> 03:13.152
and they all had sort of dark hair.

03:13.820 --> 03:14.946
And they were nice.

03:15.029 --> 03:16.030
(BUS ENGINE STARTS)

03:16.114 --> 03:17.657
They didn't dress very well, though.

03:20.785 --> 03:22.036
Where's your cane, Piper?

03:22.620 --> 03:23.621
It's in my bag. Shut up.

03:24.205 --> 03:25.248
All right. Jeez.

03:25.832 --> 03:27.625
- You ask me all the time!
- Okay!

03:30.587 --> 03:31.671
How was goalball?

03:31.754 --> 03:33.089
Uh, we lost.

03:34.048 --> 03:35.466
(MUSIC PLAYING OVER CAR SPEAKERS)

03:36.676 --> 03:37.677
(SIGHS SOFTLY)

03:39.888 --> 03:41.014
- PIPER: Andy!
- Hmm?

03:41.097 --> 03:42.348
- Andy!
- Yeah?

03:42.432 --> 03:43.433
- Andy!
- What?

03:43.516 --> 03:44.893
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

03:44.976 --> 03:46.144
ANDY: Dad?

03:46.227 --> 03:47.270
(PANTING)

03:47.353 --> 03:48.438
ANDY: Dad?

03:49.981 --> 03:51.608
Dad, can you answer me, please!

03:51.691 --> 03:52.984
(PIPER PANTING)

03:53.818 --> 03:55.820
- Andy!
- Here, here, here, here, here.

03:58.156 --> 03:59.657
Dad, I'm gonna come in, okay?

03:59.741 --> 04:00.992
PIPER: He always answers.

04:01.075 --> 04:02.827
ANDY: Uh, okay, we're coming in, Dad.

04:04.829 --> 04:05.997
PIPER: Not answering!

04:06.748 --> 04:09.208
- (WATER RUNNING)
- (DOOR CREAKING)

04:11.377 --> 04:13.379
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

04:15.006 --> 04:16.007
PIPER: Dad?

04:17.175 --> 04:18.176
Dad?

04:19.260 --> 04:20.261
What's happening?

04:22.263 --> 04:23.890
Andy?

04:24.933 --> 04:26.309
(BREATH TREMBLES)

04:26.392 --> 04:27.393
Andy!

04:28.519 --> 04:29.896
What's happening?

04:35.902 --> 04:37.445
Dad?

04:37.528 --> 04:38.529
Dad!

04:39.405 --> 04:40.406
Dad!

04:41.032 --> 04:45.203
Andy! (SCREAMING)

04:46.663 --> 04:48.331
(WATER DRIPS)

04:51.459 --> 04:53.169
POLICE OFFICER: Yeah. Now, take a breath.

04:53.252 --> 04:55.380
PIPER: He'd just finished chemo. He was...

04:56.130 --> 04:57.924
He was supposed to be better.

04:58.007 --> 04:59.008
OFFICER: Okay.

04:59.092 --> 05:01.844
And, Piper, did your brother
try to help you?

05:01.928 --> 05:02.929
- No?
- (GULPS)

05:03.721 --> 05:05.223
PIPER: He didn't want me in there.

05:05.306 --> 05:06.307
OFFICER: Okay.

05:06.391 --> 05:08.059
PIPER: He told me Dad would be okay.

05:09.060 --> 05:11.229
- OFFICER: Okay, that's okay.
- (STRETCHER RATTLES)

05:11.312 --> 05:13.648
That's okay. You've been so brave, Piper.

05:15.566 --> 05:17.068
MAN: Lift it up a little bit. Just...

05:17.944 --> 05:19.153
(SIGHS WEARILY)

05:21.155 --> 05:24.033
(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

05:25.284 --> 05:26.744
WOMAN: Hmm.

05:27.412 --> 05:31.499
It says here you're partially
sighted. Is that right, Piper?

05:32.834 --> 05:37.130
I can... I can only see shapes
and light. That's about it.

05:38.464 --> 05:40.800
I've talked to an amazing foster mum

05:40.883 --> 05:43.052
called Laura. You're gonna love her.

05:43.970 --> 05:47.682
And, Andy, we're gonna put you
in your own supervised unit.

05:49.976 --> 05:51.394
- What?
- Wait, hold on,

05:51.477 --> 05:52.645
you're splitting us up?

05:52.729 --> 05:53.813
ANDY: But I look after her.

05:54.814 --> 05:57.150
You can apply for guardianship
when you're 18.

05:57.233 --> 05:59.986
Okay, I-I really don't want her

06:00.069 --> 06:01.571
to move in with a stranger.

06:02.071 --> 06:03.072
She needs me.

06:03.156 --> 06:04.824
PIPER: Why can't he just come with me?

06:06.075 --> 06:07.744
Laura's had issues

06:07.827 --> 06:10.580
with troubled kids in the past, and...

06:12.248 --> 06:13.458
PIPER: What?

06:13.541 --> 06:14.751
Nothing.

06:16.294 --> 06:17.628
Grapefruit.

06:21.215 --> 06:24.302
I got into trouble when I was younger.

06:25.094 --> 06:26.929
But it was ages ago. I was, like, eight.

06:28.681 --> 06:29.766
Can you, um...

06:29.849 --> 06:31.309
(GULPS, SIGHS SOFTLY)

06:31.392 --> 06:32.602
Can you talk to her and just tell her

06:32.685 --> 06:33.895
that we are not splitting up?

06:34.437 --> 06:37.857
If she agrees, can you behave
yourself for three months?

06:48.576 --> 06:49.619
Oi.

06:53.039 --> 06:54.165
(SIGHS)

06:56.709 --> 06:57.835
You hear that?

06:57.919 --> 06:58.961
(PLANE FLIES OVERHEAD)

07:00.421 --> 07:01.756
That's Dad going to heaven.

07:02.840 --> 07:03.841
Shut up.

07:05.301 --> 07:06.636
No, seriously though, that's...

07:07.929 --> 07:09.180
That's what happens.

07:09.263 --> 07:11.474
You don't get burned or buried, you just...

07:11.557 --> 07:12.642
(INHALES)

07:13.226 --> 07:14.352
catch a plane.

07:16.229 --> 07:17.313
(PIPER CHUCKLES)

07:18.314 --> 07:20.608
You don't have to make everything
nice for me, you know.

07:22.985 --> 07:24.070
Yeah, I know.

07:25.571 --> 07:27.156
The room still smells like him.

07:27.949 --> 07:29.117
Oh, Pipe.

07:30.660 --> 07:31.869
(ANDY EXHALES DEEPLY)

07:33.162 --> 07:34.580
You could take some of his clothes.

07:36.874 --> 07:37.959
They're washed.

07:38.584 --> 07:39.627
Don't smell like him.

07:42.839 --> 07:44.090
His pillow, then.

07:44.173 --> 07:45.508
That's not been washed yet.

07:48.761 --> 07:50.263
(PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING)

08:15.913 --> 08:17.123
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

08:37.185 --> 08:38.394
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

08:40.646 --> 08:42.565
Uh, we are... here.

08:42.648 --> 08:43.733
(THUDS)

08:45.276 --> 08:46.360
Shit!

08:47.486 --> 08:48.738
PIPER: Thought I was the blind one.

08:48.821 --> 08:49.989
Oh, shut up, Piper.

08:50.072 --> 08:51.240
(PIPER LAUGHS)

08:53.201 --> 08:54.202
(ANDY SIGHS)

08:54.994 --> 08:56.204
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING IN DISTANCE)

08:59.332 --> 09:01.042
PIPER: Smells like Mum's garden used to.

09:02.752 --> 09:03.961
We're not here for long, Pipe.

09:06.255 --> 09:07.340
Come on.

09:08.966 --> 09:10.384
(<i>ALIVE</i> BY EMPIRE OF THE SUN
PLAYING LOUDLY)

09:10.468 --> 09:12.720
PIPER: (SHOUTING) Hello?
LAURA: (SHOUTING) Come in!

09:13.262 --> 09:15.723
- What?
- The door's open!

09:17.391 --> 09:19.310
Just let yourselves in.

09:20.686 --> 09:22.188
<i>♪ Can't you help me see ♪</i>

09:22.271 --> 09:23.564
LAURA: Excuse the music!

09:23.648 --> 09:24.774
Whoo!

09:24.857 --> 09:26.317
<i>♪ Loving every minute ♪</i>

09:26.400 --> 09:29.111
<i>♪ 'Cause you make me feel so alive ♪</i>

09:30.196 --> 09:31.530
<i>♪ Alive ♪</i>

09:32.615 --> 09:34.158
<i>♪ Loving every minute ♪</i>

09:34.242 --> 09:36.035
<i>♪ 'Cause you make me feel so... ♪</i>

09:36.118 --> 09:37.620
LAURA: Oh, here you are!

09:37.703 --> 09:38.996
- Oh, my God.
- (MUSIC STOPS)

09:39.080 --> 09:41.540
- Look at youse! Look at you!
- ANDY: Say hi.

09:41.624 --> 09:44.543
Oh, gorgeous. Come in! (LAUGHS)

09:44.627 --> 09:46.712
Oh, welcome to your new home!

09:46.796 --> 09:48.297
<i>Mi casa,</i> your <i>casa!</i>

09:48.381 --> 09:50.383
- I'm Laura and you're...
- Hi.

09:50.466 --> 09:51.717
- Piper?
- Yeah.

09:51.801 --> 09:53.177
And...

09:54.011 --> 09:55.137
- Andy.
- That's right.

09:55.221 --> 09:56.806
Hey, you know what we need?

09:56.889 --> 09:59.183
A photo. Yeah? Shall we get a photo?

09:59.267 --> 10:01.227
- Yeah?
- I think so. I'd love that.

10:01.310 --> 10:02.603
- Smile.
- Here. Yeah. Yeah.

10:03.104 --> 10:04.939
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY) Aah!

10:05.022 --> 10:06.357
Hey, that's great.

10:06.440 --> 10:07.942
That's lovely.

10:08.025 --> 10:09.652
Look at that. (LAUGHS)

10:09.735 --> 10:11.153
Oh, someone...

10:12.029 --> 10:13.114
needs to meet Pompom.

10:13.197 --> 10:15.199
- Oh, who's Pompom?
- That's my dog.

10:15.950 --> 10:17.159
- Yeah.
- (PIPER CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

10:17.243 --> 10:18.244
Come here.

10:20.121 --> 10:21.330
He's a bit shy.

10:22.707 --> 10:25.626
- (BARKS, LAUGHS)
- He's stuffed, Pipe.

10:25.710 --> 10:27.128
Yeah, no, he's dead.

10:27.211 --> 10:28.337
I know I'm a weirdo.

10:28.421 --> 10:31.340
(LAUGHS) Row-row, Piper! Row-row, Andy!

10:31.424 --> 10:32.675
PIPER: Hi, Pompom.

10:32.758 --> 10:34.510
LAURA: There's a house cat
around here somewhere.

10:34.593 --> 10:35.594
Junkman.

10:35.678 --> 10:37.221
Haven't stuffed him. Yet.

10:37.305 --> 10:38.931
- But I will do.
- (CHUCKLES)

10:39.724 --> 10:40.891
Where's your cane, love?

10:40.975 --> 10:43.269
Oh, I don't like using it.

10:43.352 --> 10:44.353
Oh, how come?

10:45.104 --> 10:48.190
Uh, don't want people
treating me different.

10:48.274 --> 10:49.775
LAURA: How do they treat you different?

10:49.859 --> 10:51.360
People start to baby me, so...

10:51.444 --> 10:52.570
Oh, yeah, no.

10:52.653 --> 10:54.071
People can be judgmental.

10:54.155 --> 10:56.157
But you know what my nan used to say?

10:56.991 --> 10:58.826
"Fuck off, you fat fucking fuckers."

10:58.909 --> 11:00.328
- (LAURA WHEEZES)
- (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

11:00.411 --> 11:01.537
She did!

11:01.620 --> 11:03.789
She was always swearing. I never swear.

11:03.873 --> 11:05.041
I loved her.

11:05.124 --> 11:06.584
Is this for Piper?

11:07.710 --> 11:08.961
Oh, no.

11:09.045 --> 11:10.171
My daughter's blind.

11:10.254 --> 11:11.589
ANDY: Oh, is she here?

11:13.424 --> 11:15.176
No, she's passed.

11:16.260 --> 11:17.386
Sorry.

11:17.470 --> 11:18.721
No, it's all right. You didn't know.

11:18.804 --> 11:20.514
- It's not your fault.
- How'd she die?

11:20.598 --> 11:22.350
- Piper!
- She's okay.

11:23.601 --> 11:24.727
She drowned.

11:26.479 --> 11:28.856
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)
- Oh, who's calling?

11:28.939 --> 11:30.191
Oh, it's Wendy.

11:30.816 --> 11:32.777
She is so needy.

11:32.860 --> 11:33.903
- Hello, Wendy?
<i>- The kids get in?</i>

11:33.986 --> 11:35.905
- Yeah, no, they just arrived.
<i>- You know the drill.</i>

11:35.988 --> 11:37.907
Yeah, no, all good. Yep.

11:37.990 --> 11:40.242
Make yourselves at home. Wendy says hi.

11:40.326 --> 11:41.327
- Hi, Wendy.
- Yeah?

11:41.410 --> 11:42.536
- (ANDY SNIFFLES)
- LAURA: Okay.

11:42.620 --> 11:44.205
- Does she have a backyard?
- It's a bit inconvenient.

11:44.288 --> 11:45.498
- She does have a backyard.
- Don't worry.

11:45.581 --> 11:46.665
Do you wanna see it?

11:47.666 --> 11:48.876
That's all right.

11:48.959 --> 11:50.878
Oh, bloody hell.

11:52.380 --> 11:53.547
- (MEOWS)
- Oh, if you're going outside,

11:53.631 --> 11:54.757
don't let the cat out.

11:54.840 --> 11:55.925
Oh, fuck.

11:56.759 --> 11:58.094
- Idiot.
- Piper!

11:58.844 --> 11:59.929
Right, wait here.

12:00.763 --> 12:02.056
LAURA. Yeah, no. (CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)

12:02.807 --> 12:04.433
(WHISTLES, CLICKS TONGUE)

12:05.267 --> 12:07.269
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

12:08.145 --> 12:09.688
(JUNKMAN MEOWING)

12:12.566 --> 12:14.568
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

12:17.279 --> 12:18.280
(JUNKMAN MEOWING)

12:22.952 --> 12:24.537
(JUNKMAN SHRIEKING)

12:24.620 --> 12:26.414
- Oliver! Excuse me.
- (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC ENDS)

12:26.497 --> 12:28.249
Oliver! No.

12:29.041 --> 12:30.668
Give me the cat. Give me the cat.

12:30.751 --> 12:32.128
Let him go.

12:32.211 --> 12:33.421
Got you. I got you.

12:33.504 --> 12:34.839
- Let him go, Ollie.
- PIPER: Andy.

12:35.631 --> 12:37.716
- Careful.
- LAURA: I got ya.

12:44.014 --> 12:45.015
What's happening?

12:46.767 --> 12:47.768
Um...

12:49.186 --> 12:50.521
(WHISPERING) The cat got in the pool.

12:50.604 --> 12:52.106
Laura's sorting it out, though.

12:52.189 --> 12:53.482
I think her kid's...

12:55.109 --> 12:56.110
holding it.

13:04.201 --> 13:05.286
LAURA: Yep.

13:05.953 --> 13:07.079
(INHALES) Yeah.

13:07.955 --> 13:10.749
It's your new sister and brother, Oliver.

13:11.542 --> 13:12.918
Piper and Anthony.

13:13.544 --> 13:14.712
Andy.

13:16.297 --> 13:18.924
Handy Andy. (CHUCKLES)

13:19.592 --> 13:21.927
Oliver lost his family,
just like you guys.

13:22.011 --> 13:24.138
Needed someone that could
give him special care.

13:24.221 --> 13:25.931
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

13:26.015 --> 13:27.016
You're done, darling.

13:27.558 --> 13:28.642
Oliver?

13:29.894 --> 13:30.895
Oliver.

13:31.770 --> 13:32.897
Yep, quick as you can, darling.

13:33.606 --> 13:34.982
Good lad.

13:35.065 --> 13:36.066
Here you are.

13:38.736 --> 13:42.072
Oliver's been mute, selectively mute

13:42.156 --> 13:43.574
since we lost Cathy.

13:44.658 --> 13:46.285
So we try not to overwhelm him.

13:46.368 --> 13:47.369
Isn't that right, darling?

13:47.995 --> 13:50.664
Taking one step at a time, aren't we, hmm?

13:50.748 --> 13:52.458
Okay, you're done.

13:53.751 --> 13:54.919
It's your turn.

13:57.505 --> 13:58.839
Quite tall, aren't you?

13:58.923 --> 14:00.424
What's he look like, Andy?

14:01.675 --> 14:02.885
Oh, he's cute.

14:03.677 --> 14:04.762
He's smiling at you.

14:05.763 --> 14:06.847
(CHUCKLES)

14:08.432 --> 14:10.309
- What color's his hair?
- Red.

14:11.602 --> 14:13.312
Yeah, and curly too.

14:17.650 --> 14:19.652
He's a beautiful boy.

14:21.529 --> 14:22.571
(THUDS)

14:24.865 --> 14:25.991
(SIGHS)

14:26.075 --> 14:27.451
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

14:33.249 --> 14:34.333
There we go.

14:35.000 --> 14:37.711
Good girl. And there's a wall
on your right.

14:38.379 --> 14:40.130
And straight down to your bedroom.

14:40.214 --> 14:41.882
Just watch out for this step, Pipe.

14:41.966 --> 14:43.551
LAURA: Yep, old news, Andy.

14:44.301 --> 14:45.970
- ANDY: Okay.
- Straight ahead, love.

14:46.637 --> 14:48.013
There you are.

14:48.097 --> 14:49.098
It's Cathy's room.

14:50.224 --> 14:51.350
You okay, Pipe?

14:51.433 --> 14:52.643
PIPER: Yeah, I'm okay.

14:52.726 --> 14:53.936
Grapefruit.

14:54.019 --> 14:55.229
I'm all good, Andy.

14:56.564 --> 14:59.275
Yep, sorry, uh, your room's in there.

14:59.358 --> 15:00.359
It's just up there.

15:00.442 --> 15:02.611
- Okay.
- Okay, great.

15:02.695 --> 15:04.405
(GRUNTS)

15:06.240 --> 15:07.241
(SIGHS)

15:11.453 --> 15:12.454
(WHISPERS) Fuck.

15:19.336 --> 15:20.462
(LAUGHS SOFTLY)

15:22.673 --> 15:23.882
Not much of a room.

15:25.551 --> 15:27.052
Oh, no, no, it's fine.

15:28.596 --> 15:31.807
Wendy tells me you're applying
for guardianship. That right?

15:31.890 --> 15:34.852
Yes, yeah, in, uh, three months.

15:34.935 --> 15:36.353
When I'm 18.

15:36.437 --> 15:38.772
I'm supposed to report
how safe and reliable you are.

15:39.481 --> 15:41.150
So stay safe.

15:41.233 --> 15:42.610
Stay reliable, yeah?

15:42.693 --> 15:43.694
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

15:44.903 --> 15:46.030
- (SOFTLY) Yes.
- (PHONE BEEPS)

15:46.113 --> 15:47.948
Oh, girlfriend?

15:48.032 --> 15:49.033
Oh, no.

15:50.034 --> 15:51.201
Boyfriend?

15:52.119 --> 15:53.370
Just a friend.

15:54.288 --> 15:55.748
So what are you talking about?

15:55.831 --> 15:57.082
Nothing. (CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

15:57.166 --> 15:58.167
Your dad?

15:59.585 --> 16:00.961
- No.
- (WHISPERS) Hey.

16:01.045 --> 16:03.088
(IN NORMAL VOICE) Hey, I'm a counselor.

16:04.048 --> 16:06.008
People pay to talk to me, you know.

16:06.091 --> 16:08.010
Oh. That... That's cool.

16:09.970 --> 16:12.890
So you don't have
to be so defensive, Andy.

16:14.099 --> 16:15.643
Am I... Am I being defensive?

16:15.726 --> 16:17.144
Oh, come on, look at you.

16:17.895 --> 16:18.896
Arms crossed.

16:19.688 --> 16:21.899
Clutching onto your phone
to tell me you want me to go.

16:21.982 --> 16:22.983
- (CHUCKLES)
- PIPER: Hey,

16:23.067 --> 16:24.318
- I think I can hear you guys.
- (KNOCKS ON WALL)

16:24.401 --> 16:25.402
Can you hear me?

16:26.195 --> 16:28.656
(SHOUTING) Yeah! Yeah, um...

16:28.739 --> 16:30.157
- Yeah, yeah, you okay?
- PIPER: Yep!

16:30.240 --> 16:31.700
- LAURA: She all right?
- You need anything?

16:31.784 --> 16:33.452
PIPER: Yeah, uh, a better brother?

16:34.870 --> 16:35.871
Okay.

16:37.289 --> 16:38.332
Hey.

16:38.415 --> 16:40.000
Laura! Get off my phone!
What are you doing?

16:40.084 --> 16:41.293
- (OBJECT CLATTERS)
- (GASPING) Sorry.

16:42.378 --> 16:44.880
- I'm so sorry.
- No, I'm... Uh, I'm sorry.

16:44.963 --> 16:46.548
No, you're all right. It's my bad.

16:46.632 --> 16:48.092
I just don't like people
going through my stuff.

16:48.175 --> 16:50.010
Absolutely, it's just you had a message.

16:50.719 --> 16:51.720
I didn't mean to yell.

16:53.305 --> 16:54.306
Cool.

17:00.604 --> 17:02.439
So Oliver's a fucking weirdo, is he?

17:06.318 --> 17:07.611
No.

17:08.195 --> 17:09.405
Oh.

17:09.488 --> 17:10.489
Excuse me.

17:12.950 --> 17:14.326
(SIGHS)

17:15.119 --> 17:16.328
Oh, fuck.

17:18.080 --> 17:19.957
(<i>THE RIOT</i> BY VIOLENCE PLAYING)

17:31.844 --> 17:33.512
(GRUNTING)

17:36.557 --> 17:37.558
(MUFFLED MUSIC CONTINUES)

17:57.286 --> 17:59.163
(EERIE MUSIC PLAYING)

18:05.544 --> 18:06.962
(LAURA EXHALES)

18:10.340 --> 18:11.925
(EXHALES)

18:14.845 --> 18:16.722
(WHISTLING)

18:16.805 --> 18:18.807
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

18:27.524 --> 18:28.859
(TINKLING)

18:35.282 --> 18:36.450
LAURA: (WHISPERS) Wait in your room.

18:51.924 --> 18:53.926
(VCR WHIRRING)

18:57.846 --> 18:59.181
(T.V. STATIC HISSING)

19:00.265 --> 19:01.475
(WOMAN CRYING)

19:02.768 --> 19:03.769
(GASPING)

19:12.903 --> 19:13.904
(WOMAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

19:17.157 --> 19:19.076
(WOMAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

19:25.457 --> 19:27.042
(JUNKMAN MEOWING)

19:29.628 --> 19:30.629
(GRUNTS)

19:34.800 --> 19:36.134
(SIGHS IN EXASPERATION)

20:00.826 --> 20:03.453
- (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)
- (BIRDS CHIRPING)

20:40.157 --> 20:42.034
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

20:44.161 --> 20:46.038
- (FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)
- (KNOCK ON DOOR)

20:46.121 --> 20:47.164
- (GASPS)
- LAURA: Up you get!

20:48.040 --> 20:49.041
(GROANS SOFTLY)

20:51.293 --> 20:52.794
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDE)

20:52.878 --> 20:53.879
Ugh.

20:56.048 --> 20:57.049
(SIGHS)

20:58.800 --> 21:00.135
Oh, you...

21:01.678 --> 21:03.555
(WASHING MACHINE WHIRRING)

21:14.232 --> 21:15.233
(WHIRRING STOPS)

21:15.317 --> 21:16.652
(WATER SPLASHING)

21:18.403 --> 21:20.280
(SHOWER RUNNING)

21:26.620 --> 21:27.621
PIPER: (WHISPERS) <i>Dad.</i>

21:28.580 --> 21:29.706
<i>I wanna come too.</i>

21:29.790 --> 21:31.166
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

21:32.834 --> 21:34.336
PIPER: (SHOUTING) <i>Andy!</i>

21:34.419 --> 21:35.545
<i>Andy!</i>

21:35.629 --> 21:36.630
(PANTING)

21:38.340 --> 21:39.883
<i>No, please!</i>

21:39.967 --> 21:41.134
<i>Please!</i>

21:42.052 --> 21:43.679
(SHOWER RUNNING)

22:00.487 --> 22:01.488
Hey, Ollie.

22:02.823 --> 22:04.032
We're going out for a little bit.

22:05.033 --> 22:06.034
You'll be all right?

22:08.829 --> 22:09.830
Good.

22:11.498 --> 22:13.834
(KEYS JINGLE, LOCK CLICKS)

22:13.917 --> 22:15.919
(<i>BOSTON</i> BY DERMOT KENNEDY PLAYING)

22:16.003 --> 22:17.587
PIPER: (WHISPERS) <i>What's he look like?</i>

22:18.922 --> 22:22.342
<i>♪ We were swimming out so far this time ♪</i>

22:22.426 --> 22:23.427
He looks good.

22:26.138 --> 22:27.139
Grapefruit.

22:29.725 --> 22:30.726
He looks good, Pipe.

22:35.188 --> 22:37.607
<i>♪ Pretty intimate so far ♪</i>

22:37.691 --> 22:39.359
<i>♪ So I ♪</i>

22:42.029 --> 22:43.238
PIPER: (SOFTLY) Goodbye, Dad.

22:45.157 --> 22:46.199
ANDY: Thank you.

22:46.283 --> 22:47.701
- Sorry for your loss.
- PIPER: Thank you.

23:13.143 --> 23:15.729
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

23:21.818 --> 23:23.236
LAURA: Andy, sorry.

23:23.779 --> 23:24.780
ANDY: Mm.

23:25.989 --> 23:27.407
Andy, I can't let you do this.

23:28.075 --> 23:29.076
What?

23:29.826 --> 23:31.995
Leave without saying goodbye.

23:32.996 --> 23:35.248
Okay? It's the last time
you'll be able to look at him.

23:35.332 --> 23:36.666
PIPER: You didn't look at him?

23:39.586 --> 23:41.588
You said he looked good.

23:42.631 --> 23:43.632
Pipe.

23:45.175 --> 23:47.052
I said, "Grapefruit."

23:47.135 --> 23:49.262
I didn't want to see him like that, Pipe.

23:49.346 --> 23:51.264
LAURA: It's better than
how you saw him last.

23:54.476 --> 23:55.811
Look, some people believe

23:55.894 --> 23:58.522
the spirit stays in the body
for months after death.

24:00.065 --> 24:02.067
If that's true, then he's still in there.

24:03.777 --> 24:05.695
(COLLAR JINGLING)

24:09.074 --> 24:10.450
(DOOR THUDS)

24:13.370 --> 24:14.663
(THUDDING CONTINUES)

24:15.872 --> 24:16.957
(MEOWS)

24:20.252 --> 24:21.253
(THUDS)

24:27.509 --> 24:29.094
(GLASS SHATTERING)

24:37.561 --> 24:40.147
(LOUD THUDDING)

24:47.571 --> 24:49.573
(CHICKENS CLUCKING IN DISTANCE)

24:53.243 --> 24:55.203
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

25:01.877 --> 25:03.587
(CHITTERS)

25:08.091 --> 25:10.302
(ANDY BREATHING HEAVILY)

25:12.721 --> 25:13.722
LAURA: You see?

25:15.891 --> 25:16.892
He's so peaceful.

25:19.186 --> 25:20.187
Yep.

25:21.646 --> 25:22.647
(GULPS SOFTLY)

25:22.731 --> 25:24.357
You should kiss him goodbye.

25:26.985 --> 25:28.403
(BREATH TREMBLING)

25:29.321 --> 25:30.322
No.

25:31.907 --> 25:33.742
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

25:39.581 --> 25:40.790
(SIGHS WEARILY) No.

25:46.421 --> 25:47.756
Kiss your father, Andy.

25:51.301 --> 25:52.302
It's a custom.

25:54.387 --> 25:56.306
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

26:02.103 --> 26:03.104
(SNIFFLES)

26:03.688 --> 26:04.689
(WHISPERS) There we go.

26:11.738 --> 26:12.739
His lips.

26:14.574 --> 26:15.700
(SHUDDERS)

26:15.784 --> 26:17.994
Yeah. It's custom.

26:18.620 --> 26:20.330
- It's not.
- It is, darling.

26:21.039 --> 26:22.040
It is.

26:22.749 --> 26:23.750
Let me help you.

26:25.168 --> 26:26.169
Come on.

26:26.670 --> 26:28.588
- I can't.
- It's okay, it's okay.

26:28.672 --> 26:30.799
- I can't do that.
- It's okay, I've got you.

26:30.882 --> 26:31.883
I've got you.

26:32.842 --> 26:33.843
Yeah?

26:37.013 --> 26:39.015
Don't worry, you're in good hands.

26:39.099 --> 26:40.100
(ANDY SIGHS)

26:43.144 --> 26:44.396
(ANDY SHUDDERS)

26:52.112 --> 26:54.906
(TUTS) Oh, come on, it doesn't
have to be like this.

26:55.865 --> 26:57.617
Seriously, a funeral isn't
supposed to be all misery.

26:57.701 --> 26:59.536
It's supposed to be a celebration.

27:00.245 --> 27:02.455
Let's have some fun, huh?

27:04.499 --> 27:06.876
Piper, what do you do for fun, eh?

27:07.877 --> 27:09.337
Kick Andy in the balls.

27:10.672 --> 27:12.173
(LAUGHS WHIMSICALLY)

27:12.257 --> 27:13.675
Yes!

27:16.261 --> 27:18.680
What about you, Andy?
What do you like to do?

27:19.764 --> 27:20.932
Huh?

27:21.016 --> 27:22.309
I don't know. Get hammered.

27:23.310 --> 27:24.936
Hammered? Okay.

27:26.146 --> 27:27.272
Well, let's get hammered.

27:27.355 --> 27:30.233
(LIVELY ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

27:30.317 --> 27:32.402
- (INDISTINCT CHATTERING)
- LAURA: This one?

27:41.828 --> 27:43.246
<i>♪ Now, listen ♪</i>

27:45.582 --> 27:46.791
(DOOR RATTLING)

27:47.792 --> 27:49.419
ANDY: <i>So, the game is called Odds On.</i>

27:49.502 --> 27:51.463
You've got to pick a number
between one and ten.

27:51.546 --> 27:52.589
- Yep.
- You got one?

27:52.672 --> 27:53.923
Seven.

27:54.007 --> 27:55.383
Well, no, you're not meant
to say it out loud yet.

27:55.467 --> 27:56.718
- LAURA: Oh!
- Yeah, keep it in your head.

27:56.801 --> 27:59.304
Now, on the count of three,
you do say it out loud...

27:59.387 --> 28:01.097
and then if I guess your number,

28:01.181 --> 28:03.058
- you have to drink.
- Got it.

28:03.141 --> 28:04.893
Piper, hit us with the countdown.

28:04.976 --> 28:06.936
Mm-hm. Three, two, one.

28:07.020 --> 28:08.104
BOTH: Seven.

28:08.188 --> 28:09.189
(LAUGHS)

28:09.272 --> 28:10.940
- Why'd you say it again?
- Bloody cheater!

28:11.024 --> 28:13.485
- All right, it doesn't matter.
- That was so stupid.

28:13.568 --> 28:14.611
- I can take a shot.
- Okay.

28:14.694 --> 28:15.695
- Ready?
- Yeah.

28:15.779 --> 28:16.780
- Ready?
- Yeah.

28:18.865 --> 28:20.575
(MAKES CHOKING SOUNDS)

28:20.658 --> 28:22.035
(GURGLES)

28:22.118 --> 28:23.203
ANDY: Oh, no!

28:23.286 --> 28:25.580
- (LAUGHING)
- LAURA: All right, I'm sorry.

28:26.373 --> 28:27.999
All right, Piper, Odds On.

28:28.792 --> 28:30.168
- Really?
- LAURA: Yeah!

28:30.251 --> 28:31.461
With the whiskey?

28:31.544 --> 28:32.545
(WHISPERS) Say four.

28:33.296 --> 28:35.298
Three, two, one...

28:35.924 --> 28:37.592
- BOTH: Four!
- (LAURA LAUGHS)

28:38.551 --> 28:41.554
Oh, calm down, muscles,
it's just one drink.

28:41.638 --> 28:42.639
One little drink.

28:42.722 --> 28:44.349
All right, but you're not
going to like it, Piper,

28:44.432 --> 28:45.975
- I'm telling you.
- We'll see.

28:50.855 --> 28:52.816
- Do you like it? Yeah?
- (COUGHS)

28:52.899 --> 28:55.026
- Oh, it's good, right?
- (LAURA CHUCKLES)

28:55.110 --> 28:57.278
Oh, that's disgusting, you drink that!

28:57.362 --> 28:58.405
- (BURPS)
- (LAUGHS)

28:58.488 --> 29:00.156
Yeah, I'm more of a vodka slut, eh?

29:00.240 --> 29:02.325
You go for it. I hate vodka.

29:03.576 --> 29:04.577
One for Dad.

29:07.038 --> 29:09.541
- (SIGHS) Yeah, okay.
- Hm.

29:09.624 --> 29:11.167
- Piper?
- Yes.

29:13.253 --> 29:14.629
All right, but last one.

29:14.712 --> 29:16.464
(WHISPERING) First one.

29:16.548 --> 29:18.425
- (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)
- LAURA: Cheers.

29:18.508 --> 29:19.884
Cheers.

29:21.511 --> 29:22.512
(<i>FREAKS</i> BY TIMMY TRUMPET PLAYING)

29:22.595 --> 29:24.514
Piper, come on, I need back up!

29:24.597 --> 29:25.598
- I need back up, Piper!
- LAURA: Come on!

29:25.682 --> 29:27.058
- Piper, get over here!
- This is it!

29:27.642 --> 29:28.768
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

29:28.852 --> 29:29.853
<i>♪ Tell me ♪</i>

29:29.936 --> 29:31.271
<i>♪ Tell me ♪</i>

29:31.354 --> 29:32.689
<i>♪ Where the freaks at ♪</i>

29:32.772 --> 29:34.524
<i>♪ Freaks at, freaks at ♪</i>

29:34.607 --> 29:36.443
<i>♪ Tell me</i>
<i>Where the freaks at ♪</i>

29:44.159 --> 29:45.160
(CLUCKING)

29:47.662 --> 29:49.080
LAURA: Okay.

29:49.164 --> 29:50.665
ANDY: Oh, my God!

29:55.628 --> 29:57.380
- Bedtime, young lady. Yes!
- No!

29:57.464 --> 29:58.840
(<i>FREAKS</i> BY TIMMY TRUMPET ENDS)

29:58.923 --> 30:00.717
- LAURA: What's next?
- Andy, play Dad's song!

30:00.800 --> 30:02.594
- Yeah, play Dad's song!
- Oh!

30:02.677 --> 30:05.054
ALL: (SINGING)
<i>♪ What about me? ♪</i>

30:05.638 --> 30:07.182
<i>♪ It isn't fair ♪</i>

30:07.265 --> 30:10.768
<i>♪ I've had enough</i>
<i>Now I want my share ♪</i>

30:10.852 --> 30:12.103
<i>♪ Can't you see? ♪</i>

30:13.188 --> 30:14.230
<i>♪ I wanna live ♪</i>

30:15.231 --> 30:17.567
<i>♪ But you just take more ♪</i>

30:17.650 --> 30:20.361
<i>♪ What about me? ♪</i>

30:20.445 --> 30:22.447
- LAURA: Piper, sing it!
- (SCREAMS)

30:23.781 --> 30:25.074
(SCREAMS) ♪ <i>What about me? ♪</i>

30:25.158 --> 30:27.452
LAURA: No! Sing it properly!

30:27.535 --> 30:29.787
(ALL LAUGHING)

30:29.871 --> 30:31.164
(IN DEEP VOICE) Sing it!

30:31.247 --> 30:32.373
Sing it, Piper!

30:32.457 --> 30:33.875
(SNORING)

30:39.714 --> 30:41.716
- You've still got one left.
- Yeah.

30:45.595 --> 30:46.596
Whoops!

30:47.180 --> 30:48.515
(LAURA GRUNTS)

30:49.891 --> 30:50.892
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

30:51.476 --> 30:52.894
Thank you for today, Laura.

30:53.561 --> 30:54.687
It's okay, Andy.

30:57.357 --> 30:58.358
I've been through it.

31:01.778 --> 31:03.196
Don't you want to talk about him?

31:04.072 --> 31:05.073
Yeah, but it's...

31:05.573 --> 31:06.783
- I don't know, it's hard.
- Well...

31:09.452 --> 31:11.037
we don't have to look at each other.

31:12.872 --> 31:15.583
(CHAIRS CREAKING)

31:16.918 --> 31:17.919
Yeah, you can...

31:20.004 --> 31:21.297
ask me something.

31:21.381 --> 31:22.382
(ANDY SIGHS)

31:24.801 --> 31:25.802
You can ask me anything.

31:28.096 --> 31:29.514
How did you, um...

31:29.597 --> 31:30.598
How did you cope...

31:33.184 --> 31:35.019
with Cathy being gone?

31:35.979 --> 31:36.980
Oh.

31:38.565 --> 31:39.732
I didn't.

31:42.610 --> 31:44.237
When we buried her, I, um...

31:49.117 --> 31:50.535
I didn't want to leave...

31:51.869 --> 31:53.997
'cause it felt like I was abandoning her.

31:54.998 --> 31:55.999
You know?

31:58.960 --> 32:00.336
Mmm.

32:03.298 --> 32:05.550
How could I go home without my daughter?

32:07.176 --> 32:08.595
(SHUDDERS SOFTLY)

32:15.935 --> 32:18.563
How could I sleep in a bed
when she was in the ground?

32:29.240 --> 32:31.451
I used to stay at the cemetery for days...

32:36.456 --> 32:38.458
just so I could feel close to her.

32:41.127 --> 32:42.128
ANDY: Yeah.

32:51.054 --> 32:52.096
(SIGHS)

32:54.349 --> 32:57.185
I'd give anything to hear her
call me Mum one more time.

33:01.814 --> 33:03.024
Just one more time.

33:08.321 --> 33:09.322
That's all.

33:17.330 --> 33:18.539
You know, we'd only, uh...

33:20.291 --> 33:22.960
we'd only ever talk if it was about Piper.

33:23.836 --> 33:25.254
LAURA: Because she was the favorite, huh?

33:25.338 --> 33:26.339
(ANDY CHUCKLES)

33:27.340 --> 33:28.800
Yeah, how could she not be?

33:32.595 --> 33:33.930
Is that why you hit her?

33:40.520 --> 33:41.938
- Who told you that?
- Oh.

33:44.357 --> 33:45.358
Wendy.

33:50.446 --> 33:51.781
Were you jealous of her?

33:54.534 --> 33:57.036
(SIGHS) When my... When my dad...

33:58.162 --> 33:59.330
married her mum...

34:02.542 --> 34:03.960
(EXHALES)

34:05.044 --> 34:08.047
...it felt like he finally found the family...

34:08.923 --> 34:10.591
he actually wanted.

34:11.801 --> 34:13.052
I used to get in trouble at school

34:13.136 --> 34:16.806
just so that he'd notice me
and he... he hated me for it.

34:16.889 --> 34:18.057
(SIGHS)

34:18.141 --> 34:19.142
He'd turn on the shower

34:19.225 --> 34:20.852
so Piper couldn't hear and he'd...

34:23.479 --> 34:25.106
He used to hit me so hard...

34:27.734 --> 34:28.943
I'd wake up and...

34:33.698 --> 34:34.907
I wouldn't even know where I was.

34:34.991 --> 34:36.617
(BREATH TREMBLING)

34:36.701 --> 34:37.994
That's awful, Andy.

34:39.662 --> 34:40.830
And you know what?

34:42.832 --> 34:43.833
(INHALES)

34:46.294 --> 34:47.503
He never touched her...

34:49.213 --> 34:50.214
once.

34:52.008 --> 34:53.885
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

35:04.103 --> 35:05.730
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

35:17.492 --> 35:18.493
LAURA: You awake?

36:17.426 --> 36:19.303
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

36:30.356 --> 36:31.357
Andy?

36:42.910 --> 36:44.871
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC INTENSIFIES)

37:03.180 --> 37:05.016
(JUNKMAN MEOWING)

37:10.688 --> 37:11.689
(GASPS)

37:18.988 --> 37:19.989
(JUNKMAN MEOWS)

37:22.408 --> 37:23.409
(WATER SPLASHING)

37:25.077 --> 37:26.078
LAURA: I know you're hungry.

37:26.954 --> 37:28.915
You just have to wait a bit longer, okay?

37:35.004 --> 37:36.005
Are you in there?

37:38.633 --> 37:39.842
Is this part of it?

37:42.428 --> 37:43.804
Did I do it right?

37:47.099 --> 37:49.101
(EXHALING)

37:54.982 --> 37:56.359
How can I believe you're in there

37:56.442 --> 37:57.652
if I can't see you?

38:00.446 --> 38:01.989
(LAURA'S BREATH TREMBLING)

38:02.949 --> 38:04.992
- (RATTLING)
- (WATER RUNNING)

38:05.076 --> 38:06.077
(GASPS)

38:11.666 --> 38:13.250
(JUNKMAN MEOWS)

38:19.590 --> 38:20.591
(MEOWING CONTINUES)

38:24.387 --> 38:27.348
- (JUNKMAN GROWLING)
- (BREATHING SHALLOWLY)

38:34.480 --> 38:35.523
(JUNKMAN YOWLS RASPINGLY)

38:35.606 --> 38:37.608
- (SHATTERS)
- (SCREAMS)

38:40.820 --> 38:41.821
(GROANS)

38:46.200 --> 38:47.994
Oh, fuck!

38:52.581 --> 38:53.582
(GROANS)

39:11.809 --> 39:13.269
- Oh.
- Andy!

39:14.562 --> 39:15.563
- Is that dirty?
- PIPER: Morning, Andy!

39:15.646 --> 39:17.023
I'm putting a wash on before we head out.

39:17.106 --> 39:19.108
- No, I'll come back.
- I'm not wasting water, Andy.

39:19.191 --> 39:20.401
- No...
- Let's see what you've got.

39:20.484 --> 39:21.736
PIPER: Andy's hungover!

39:24.822 --> 39:27.033
- You going out?
- Yeah, girl shopping.

39:27.116 --> 39:29.618
- Sorry, just the two of us.
- Yeah, no boys allowed.

39:29.702 --> 39:32.038
- Oh, keep Ollie in his room.
- Mm-hm.

39:32.121 --> 39:34.123
He's mucking around
and doing my head right in.

39:34.206 --> 39:35.207
Yep.

39:35.833 --> 39:37.084
LAURA: Oh.

39:39.503 --> 39:40.504
Piss.

39:40.588 --> 39:41.756
(PIPER CHUCKLES)

39:42.882 --> 39:44.425
I don't know what... what happened.

39:45.134 --> 39:46.469
Andy, seriously?

39:48.304 --> 39:49.513
(SIGHS)

39:49.597 --> 39:50.598
LAURA: Hey.

39:52.975 --> 39:54.602
Why don't you try and take a shower?

39:57.521 --> 39:58.522
Okay.

39:59.482 --> 40:00.483
Um...

40:01.025 --> 40:02.651
- Sorry.
- LAURA: You're all right?

40:05.154 --> 40:07.490
Oh, your brother's
not very well, I don't think.

40:09.283 --> 40:10.493
I'm quite concerned.

40:11.744 --> 40:13.412
Became quite aggressive last night.

40:14.330 --> 40:15.623
I'll tell you about it in the car.

40:16.373 --> 40:18.793
(VEHICLE DRIVING AWAY)

40:22.129 --> 40:24.131
(DOOR CREAKING)

40:27.676 --> 40:28.677
(GASPS)

40:40.106 --> 40:41.107
(SIGHS)

40:44.568 --> 40:45.569
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

40:53.244 --> 40:55.246
(FLY BUZZES)

40:57.164 --> 40:58.290
(THUDS)

41:10.719 --> 41:12.721
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

41:22.857 --> 41:24.066
(DOOR RATTLES)

41:28.404 --> 41:29.613
She lock you in, Ollie?

41:48.507 --> 41:50.342
- (FLY BUZZES)
- You hungry?

41:53.220 --> 41:56.432
How long you been like this,
mute, or whatever?

41:57.975 --> 41:58.976
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

42:04.481 --> 42:05.691
You wanna write?

42:06.567 --> 42:08.527
I think you should, actually.

42:08.611 --> 42:11.322
So then, uh... then I can...
then I can talk to you.

42:13.574 --> 42:15.326
And you can talk to me.

42:22.249 --> 42:24.543
Okay, well, Ollie, this fruit is not free.

42:25.502 --> 42:26.921
It's gonna cost you some writing.

42:33.552 --> 42:34.553
There we go.

42:49.068 --> 42:50.069
Here.

42:51.320 --> 42:53.405
Careful. Just take the fruit, Ollie.

42:56.408 --> 42:58.369
Okay, I'm gonna get you a plate.

42:59.453 --> 43:01.664
I don't want Laura yelling at me...

43:02.414 --> 43:04.416
- (SIGHS)...for making a mess.
- (RAPID CLINKING)

43:05.501 --> 43:06.961
- (GASPS)
- (CLINKING)

43:08.128 --> 43:09.129
Ollie!

43:09.213 --> 43:10.381
Ollie! Ollie!

43:10.464 --> 43:12.007
Hey, hey! Ollie, Ollie, Ollie!

43:12.091 --> 43:14.343
- Stop! Stop! Stop!
- (GROANING)

43:14.426 --> 43:16.053
- (SQUELCHING)
- Stop!

43:18.597 --> 43:19.807
Fuck! Fuck!

43:20.391 --> 43:21.392
Come on!

43:21.475 --> 43:22.810
(PANTING)

43:22.893 --> 43:24.103
Come on! Come on!

43:24.186 --> 43:25.646
Hey, come on! Ollie! Ollie!

43:25.729 --> 43:27.147
What are you doing?

43:27.231 --> 43:28.732
We need to go to the hospital, okay?

43:28.816 --> 43:30.734
Come on, just follow me. It's okay.

43:30.818 --> 43:32.820
- Just come on! Ollie! Come on!
- (OLIVER GRUNTING)

43:32.903 --> 43:33.988
(OLIVER SCREAMS)

43:34.488 --> 43:35.489
Shit!

43:35.572 --> 43:38.117
(SCREAMING)

43:40.661 --> 43:42.788
Hey, look at me.
What's wrong? What's wrong?

43:42.871 --> 43:44.581
- Hey, hey. Hey!
- (GASPING, CHOKING)

43:44.665 --> 43:47.876
- Fuck, Ollie! Hey, hey, hey.
- (COUGHING)

43:47.960 --> 43:49.837
- Breathe, breathe, breathe!
- (SCREAMS)

43:52.047 --> 43:54.049
(CHOKING)

43:55.342 --> 43:56.427
Ollie.

43:57.136 --> 43:58.554
Ollie.

43:58.637 --> 44:00.764
(OLIVER CONTINUES GROANING)

44:01.598 --> 44:02.766
(LOUD THROBBING)

44:08.939 --> 44:10.566
(GASPING)

44:12.192 --> 44:13.193
Help me.

44:15.446 --> 44:16.822
(TIRES SCREECH)

44:17.948 --> 44:19.158
What's going on?

44:19.908 --> 44:22.953
Why is he outside? No, no, no, no!

44:23.037 --> 44:24.455
Get away! Get away!

44:24.538 --> 44:26.498
- Why is he outside?
- (GASPS)

44:26.582 --> 44:27.958
Get your sister inside now!

44:28.042 --> 44:29.209
- Piper, come inside.
- Andy. Andy!

44:29.293 --> 44:31.128
- Piper!
- What the heck is going on?

44:31.211 --> 44:33.756
- Just take her inside now!
- ANDY: He hurt himself.

44:33.839 --> 44:36.133
- PIPER: What?
- LAURA: Why is he outside?

44:36.216 --> 44:39.219
(MUFFLED) Andy, what happened?
What did you... Andy!

44:40.304 --> 44:41.930
Why is Laura screaming?

44:42.765 --> 44:44.183
Do I call an ambulance?

44:44.266 --> 44:46.518
LAURA: (MUFFLED) Piper, no!
I can fix this!

44:46.602 --> 44:48.312
(ANDY WHIMPERING)

44:54.401 --> 44:56.070
PIPER: It's okay, it's okay.

44:56.153 --> 44:58.030
Shh, it's all right.

44:58.947 --> 45:01.325
You're okay. You're okay.

45:01.408 --> 45:02.409
(EXHALES)

45:03.118 --> 45:04.703
(IN NORMAL VOICE) Andy, we can help you.

45:06.580 --> 45:07.956
Laura wants to get you help.

45:14.088 --> 45:15.089
ANDY: What?

45:19.635 --> 45:21.804
(WOMAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

45:25.099 --> 45:26.475
(VHS WHIRRING)

45:26.558 --> 45:29.353
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

45:31.438 --> 45:33.565
(WOMAN GASPING ON TV)

45:33.649 --> 45:34.650
You're all right.

45:36.693 --> 45:37.694
OLIVER: Where am I?

45:41.698 --> 45:43.742
(BREATH TREMBLING)

45:46.161 --> 45:47.162
Who are you?

45:47.246 --> 45:49.373
- What?
- What do you want?

45:49.456 --> 45:52.084
- Shh!
- Please! No!

45:52.167 --> 45:54.086
It's all right, Ollie, it's all right!

45:54.169 --> 45:55.504
- Let's get you bandaged up!
- (LOUD MUSIC PLAYING)

45:55.587 --> 45:57.339
You're all right. Shh!

45:57.423 --> 45:58.590
(LOUD MUSIC CONTINUES MUTED)

45:58.674 --> 46:01.260
It's okay. It's okay,
it's okay. It's okay.

46:01.844 --> 46:02.845
OLIVER: (SCREAMS) Help!

46:03.846 --> 46:05.889
(OLIVER SCREAMING)

46:08.517 --> 46:09.601
You're all right!

46:09.685 --> 46:11.562
No. No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

46:11.645 --> 46:13.439
It's all right! No, no, no, no, no!

46:13.522 --> 46:14.523
Stay. Stay!

46:15.399 --> 46:17.568
You're all right, love. You're all right!

46:18.444 --> 46:19.903
No, no, no, no, no.

46:19.987 --> 46:22.114
You're all right. You're all right.

46:22.197 --> 46:23.740
- You're okay.
- (MUFFLED SCREAMING)

46:23.824 --> 46:26.743
You're okay now! Shh! You're okay.

46:26.827 --> 46:28.704
(MUFFLED MUSIC CONTINUES)

46:31.373 --> 46:33.000
- (OLIVER GROANS)
- Shhh.

46:34.877 --> 46:35.878
ANDY: Laura?

46:36.545 --> 46:37.921
(MOUTHING) There we go.

46:38.005 --> 46:39.006
ANDY: Is Oliver okay?

46:39.798 --> 46:41.341
(MOUTHING) You're all right.

46:41.425 --> 46:42.551
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

46:47.806 --> 46:48.807
ANDY: Laura?

46:51.143 --> 46:52.728
PIPER: Hey, Laura!

46:54.188 --> 46:55.856
- ANDY: Laura?
- PIPER: Laura!

46:55.939 --> 46:57.357
ANDY: He said he needs help.

46:59.026 --> 47:00.027
(MUSIC STOPS)

47:00.110 --> 47:01.653
Should we take him to a hospital or...

47:03.322 --> 47:04.531
So you broke into my room?

47:06.408 --> 47:07.826
Respect my fucking privacy!

47:10.162 --> 47:11.580
Come on, love. You're all right.

47:12.456 --> 47:13.874
PIPER: Please don't be too mad at him.

47:16.210 --> 47:17.211
(DOOR SLAMS)

47:22.966 --> 47:23.967
PIPER: Will he be okay?

47:24.593 --> 47:25.761
LAURA: Yeah, he'll be fine.

47:27.387 --> 47:29.014
Got to him just in time.

47:29.932 --> 47:30.933
Is he sick?

47:31.517 --> 47:32.643
He'll be all right now.

47:34.895 --> 47:36.480
It's Junkman I'm worried about.

47:38.357 --> 47:39.650
Think your brother let him out.

47:44.196 --> 47:45.614
PIPER: Junkman!

47:49.660 --> 47:51.078
<i>Junkman!</i>

47:54.498 --> 47:55.916
<i>Junkman!</i>

47:58.710 --> 48:00.128
<i>Junkman!</i>

48:03.924 --> 48:06.009
(WATER SPLASHING)

48:18.814 --> 48:20.107
(EXHALES HEAVILY)

48:26.029 --> 48:27.030
(RATTLES)

48:42.504 --> 48:43.505
(GASPS)

48:49.553 --> 48:50.554
MAN: (MUFFLED) Rain.

48:53.974 --> 48:55.976
She'll die in the rain.

49:01.523 --> 49:02.941
(BREATHES WEAKLY)

49:16.997 --> 49:18.624
(WHIMPERING)

49:19.625 --> 49:20.626
ANDY: Dad.

49:23.420 --> 49:24.671
(GRUNTS)

49:33.805 --> 49:35.682
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

49:39.978 --> 49:41.605
(CHITTERING)

49:44.733 --> 49:46.526
- (GASPS)
- DOCTOR 1: Nice deep breaths.

49:46.610 --> 49:47.986
Focus on the light. That's it.

49:48.070 --> 49:49.946
DOCTOR 2: Just breathe
normally. That's it.

49:50.030 --> 49:51.198
DOCTOR 1: Two...

49:51.281 --> 49:53.742
DOCTOR 2: Now, this time,
I want you to push on my hands

49:53.825 --> 49:55.243
with your feet as hard as you can, mate.

49:55.327 --> 49:56.328
ANDY: What...

49:57.913 --> 49:59.247
ANDY: What's that sound?

49:59.331 --> 50:00.957
(RAIN PATTERING)

50:01.041 --> 50:02.417
(ANDY BREATHING HEAVILY)

50:02.501 --> 50:04.211
I need... I need to go home.

50:04.294 --> 50:05.504
- I need to go home!
- Hey, hey. No, mate.

50:05.587 --> 50:06.588
Hey, hey, it's all right.

50:06.672 --> 50:07.673
- She's...
- Nurse, nurse!

50:07.756 --> 50:08.799
- She's gonna die!
- Nurse!

50:08.882 --> 50:10.634
- NURSE: Yep, yep.
- My sister's gonna die!

50:10.717 --> 50:12.552
- Hey, hey.
- Fuck. Give me the fuckin'...

50:12.636 --> 50:14.471
(ANDY YELLING INDISTINCTLY)

50:16.682 --> 50:19.976
- Get off me! Get off me!
- DOCTOR: Andy.

50:20.060 --> 50:21.103
- Andy!
- Calm down.

50:21.186 --> 50:23.188
(THUNDER RUMBLING, RAIN PATTERING)

50:42.833 --> 50:45.836
(A.I. VOICE SPEAKING)

50:50.340 --> 50:52.342
<i>Message: Laura said</i>
<i>you don't want visitors.</i>

50:52.426 --> 50:53.635
<i>Hope you're okay. Miss you.</i>

50:53.719 --> 50:54.928
<i>Miss you less than three...</i>

50:55.011 --> 50:57.013
(THUNDER RUMBLING, RAIN PATTERING)

51:00.892 --> 51:03.061
(LAUGHTER, INDISTINCT CHATTER ON SCREEN)

51:14.823 --> 51:16.783
(LAURA SOBBING)

51:17.868 --> 51:19.828
- Laura?
- Hey.

51:21.079 --> 51:22.622
I'm worried about Andy.

51:22.706 --> 51:23.707
I couldn't sleep.

51:24.207 --> 51:25.667
Me neither.

51:25.751 --> 51:26.752
Come in, love.

51:27.377 --> 51:29.379
Follow my voice? Straight ahead.

51:30.505 --> 51:31.506
I've got you.

51:33.592 --> 51:34.593
Sit here.

51:35.469 --> 51:36.470
- You all right?
- (SNIFFLES)

51:40.932 --> 51:42.642
- Oh.
- You're upset.

51:42.726 --> 51:45.312
Yeah, it's the rain. Cathy loved it.

51:46.146 --> 51:48.023
The sound, the smell.

51:53.236 --> 51:54.780
PIPER: That her on the T.V.?

51:55.655 --> 51:56.782
LAURA: Yeah, that's her.

51:58.492 --> 52:00.827
- Can we keep watching?
- Yeah, sure.

52:00.911 --> 52:02.746
(INDISTINCT CHATTER ON T.V.)

52:05.832 --> 52:08.251
FRIEND: (ON T.V.) <i>The first</i>
<i>cat-witch ever to swim.</i>

52:08.877 --> 52:10.462
CATHY: <i>You're okay, you're okay.</i>

52:10.545 --> 52:11.755
PIPER: Can you describe her?

52:13.465 --> 52:14.883
She's 12 here.

52:17.344 --> 52:18.553
Long brown hair.

52:21.014 --> 52:22.015
Freckles.

52:26.603 --> 52:28.063
God, she's beautiful.

52:28.980 --> 52:31.066
<i>- Here, look at your ears!</i>
<i>- Oh!</i>

52:31.149 --> 52:32.150
I'm sorry.

52:32.234 --> 52:34.069
CATHY: <i>Look at my new earrings</i>
<i>Mum bought me.</i>

52:36.029 --> 52:37.030
It's all right.

52:37.989 --> 52:38.990
LAURA: <i>Thank you.</i>

52:44.788 --> 52:48.542
<i>Yeah, ah, Ollie? Ollie! Ollie!</i>

52:48.625 --> 52:50.001
<i>- Yeah?</i>
<i>- Get her cane.</i>

52:50.085 --> 52:52.128
<i>- Okay, Aunty Laura.</i>
<i>- Thank you.</i>

52:55.549 --> 52:56.842
- LAURA: Hey, Andy.
- Mm?

52:58.093 --> 52:59.219
Handy Andy.

52:59.302 --> 53:00.303
Mmm.

53:03.431 --> 53:05.350
- Hey.
- Where's... Where's Piper?

53:06.059 --> 53:07.894
She's at home with Ollie. It's okay.

53:07.978 --> 53:08.979
(ANDY SIGHS)

53:10.605 --> 53:12.399
Look, they need to keep you in
for another day.

53:12.482 --> 53:15.569
You have a concussion.
You just need to rest.

53:15.652 --> 53:16.736
ANDY: What?

53:16.820 --> 53:20.156
Yeah, they need to check
your brain isn't leaking or something.

53:20.240 --> 53:21.491
Where... Where's Piper?

53:22.659 --> 53:23.910
Where...

53:24.995 --> 53:26.538
It's okay.

53:27.622 --> 53:29.082
- Yeah?
- (SIGHS WEARILY)

53:29.165 --> 53:30.166
Shh. Shh.

53:30.250 --> 53:31.251
(SMACKS LIPS) Oh.

53:31.334 --> 53:32.878
Brought you a present.

53:33.670 --> 53:34.796
Piper got you this.

53:35.630 --> 53:37.424
Your body spray.

53:37.507 --> 53:39.342
You can't let her out, Laura.

53:40.635 --> 53:42.178
- What's that, love?
- You can't let Piper out,

53:42.262 --> 53:43.430
not while it's raining.

53:44.347 --> 53:45.724
Something could happen.

53:45.807 --> 53:47.017
Like what?

53:47.100 --> 53:48.810
I saw my dad in the shower.

53:52.522 --> 53:54.983
(SIGHS) He said something.

53:56.776 --> 53:57.986
(EXHALES)

53:58.653 --> 53:59.863
What'd he say?

54:00.947 --> 54:02.073
Andy?

54:02.782 --> 54:04.492
He said, "She'll die in the rain."

54:09.414 --> 54:12.500
You don't think it's 'cause your dad died
in the shower when I killed him?

54:17.339 --> 54:18.340
What?

54:19.007 --> 54:20.842
Your dad died in the shower.

54:21.676 --> 54:22.677
What...

54:22.761 --> 54:24.346
You're associating rain with that.

54:25.472 --> 54:27.349
(SCOFFS)

54:29.309 --> 54:30.560
What is happening to me?

54:31.770 --> 54:32.938
Hey, don't worry.

54:33.980 --> 54:35.190
I'll keep her inside.

54:37.442 --> 54:38.860
I'll keep her inside, I promise.

54:40.111 --> 54:41.237
I promise.

54:43.490 --> 54:44.491
(LAUGHS)

54:44.574 --> 54:45.784
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

54:47.118 --> 54:48.119
You can take it.

54:48.203 --> 54:49.371
(BOTH SQUEAL)

54:49.454 --> 54:51.122
(LAUGHS) It's just water!

54:51.206 --> 54:52.749
(PIPER LAUGHS)

54:53.792 --> 54:55.877
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

55:52.142 --> 55:53.810
LAURA: <i>Cathy? Cathy!</i>

55:53.893 --> 55:55.437
<i>I'm filming you!</i>

55:55.520 --> 55:56.563
- Piper!
- (MUSIC FADES)

55:59.024 --> 56:00.692
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

56:00.775 --> 56:02.027
I want to show you something.

56:03.611 --> 56:04.946
This was Cathy's favorite.

56:08.533 --> 56:09.534
Oh!

56:14.456 --> 56:15.457
You like it?

56:15.999 --> 56:18.334
Uh-huh. Thanks, Laura.

56:19.627 --> 56:21.629
Hey, you can call me Mum, if you like.

56:23.256 --> 56:24.674
Um, maybe.

56:30.055 --> 56:31.056
Hey.

56:33.475 --> 56:34.684
She always used to...

56:35.685 --> 56:37.437
wear her hair back like this.

56:39.647 --> 56:41.649
She didn't want her hair
sticking to her face

56:41.733 --> 56:43.151
or getting in her mouth.

56:48.907 --> 56:49.908
There you are.

56:58.500 --> 57:00.502
Hey, you like living here with me?

57:01.211 --> 57:02.212
PIPER: Yeah.

57:02.295 --> 57:03.880
Yeah, you're really nice.

57:05.423 --> 57:08.093
You think you like it enough
that when Andy turns 18

57:08.176 --> 57:09.594
you maybe want to stay?

57:12.180 --> 57:13.473
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

57:13.556 --> 57:15.058
Stay here when Andy goes?

57:17.852 --> 57:18.853
Yeah.

57:22.107 --> 57:23.108
I was...

57:24.400 --> 57:27.195
I was looking forward
to getting our own place.

57:27.278 --> 57:29.280
But we'd still visit you on weekends.

57:34.202 --> 57:35.203
(WHISPERS) Okay.

57:40.500 --> 57:42.502
- (SHUDDERS)
- (DOOR CREAKING OPEN)

57:48.174 --> 57:49.175
Who's that?

57:50.760 --> 57:52.137
It's just Ollie.

57:52.220 --> 57:53.972
- (CHUCKLES) Hi.
- (CLATTERING)

57:56.432 --> 57:58.059
Not just yet, my darling.

58:03.606 --> 58:05.233
I want to show you something else.

58:07.026 --> 58:08.444
- (CHUCKLES SOFTLY) Yeah.
- Yeah?

58:11.781 --> 58:12.782
This way.

58:14.450 --> 58:15.910
That's it, straight ahead.

58:21.749 --> 58:22.959
PIPER: Oh, it's cold.

58:23.042 --> 58:24.502
LAURA: Yeah, it's a freezer, love.

58:25.587 --> 58:26.838
PIPER: Feels crusty.

58:30.258 --> 58:31.426
What is that?

58:34.971 --> 58:36.723
Oh, my God, what is it?

58:38.016 --> 58:39.017
Just meat.

58:39.684 --> 58:41.561
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

58:58.453 --> 59:00.622
(THUNDER RUMBLING, RAIN PATTERING)

59:06.252 --> 59:07.253
